Allow layer-shell clients to resize before attaching their first buffer.

Mako can refine its requested height after the first configure.  Keep sending
configures while the wlroots layer surface is initialized, including this
unmapped interval.  Track actual unmap events separately because wlroots emits
unmap before resetting initialized, including during destruction.  Clear this
state only on a new initial commit; an unmapping commit is not initial.

The private tests/layer-surface-smoke.py regression covers pre-buffer resize,
unmap/remap, and removal of an exclusive surface's reserved area.

